# Deploy target — Scaleway Kubernetes (Kapsule)

Provisions the managed cluster `deploy/chart/` installs into, with
the Private Network Kapsule requires. State is remote in an Object
Storage bucket (binding spec §5); one state per environment via
workspaces. Credentials ride the environment, never a file:

```sh
export SCW_ACCESS_KEY=…            # API key, read by both configs
export SCW_SECRET_KEY=…
export SCW_DEFAULT_PROJECT_ID=…
export AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID="$SCW_ACCESS_KEY"      # the same key, for
export AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY="$SCW_SECRET_KEY"  # the S3 state backend
```

## Once per project

```sh
./bootstrap.sh    # provisions the state bucket, then `tofu init`
```

The bootstrap config keeps local state on purpose — the bucket is the
one resource that cannot live inside the remote state it hosts.
Commit `bootstrap/terraform.tfstate`; it contains no secrets.

## Per environment

```sh
tofu workspace new dev    # once per environment; `tofu workspace select` thereafter
tofu apply
```

## Deploying

The release pipeline pushes the image; the chart runs it here. Config
rides `values.yaml` → container environment — one image serves every
environment:

```sh
scw k8s kubeconfig install "$(tofu output -raw cluster_id | cut -d/ -f2)"
helm upgrade --install <%= projectName %> ../../deploy/chart \
  --set image.repository=<registry>/<%= projectName %> \
  --set image.tag=v1.2.3
```
